// MP.
//
// Message passing: one thread writes x then y; the other reads y's new value
//   and then x's old one.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence allows, RC11 allows, RC17 allows, OD-LSO allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z allows. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     MRD allows. RC11 allows it, and MRD is weaker than RC11 (zoo edge RC11 ->
//       MRD).
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC forbids. The initial store of x hb-precedes x = 1, which hb-precedes
//       the load of x that reads the initial value: weak-read-coherence.
//     PC forbids. PC is at least PRAM.
//     PRAM forbids. The reader's view keeps the writer's writes in the order
//       issued, so x = 1 precedes its load of y.
//     Causal forbids. x = 1 causally precedes y = 1.
//     Slow allows. Slow orders a writer's writes per location only, and x and y
//       are different locations.
//     POCausal allows. Per object, the load of x has not seen x = 1: nothing at
//       location x relates them.
//     RYW allows. The reader wrote nothing, so read-your-writes asks nothing of
//       it.
//     MR allows. The two loads are of different locations, so what the first
//       saw does not constrain the second's value.
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//     WFR allows. The writer reads nothing and the reader writes nothing, so
//       writes-follow-reads orders nothing.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: none. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r0 := y;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0) [Coherence, RC11, RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, MRD, Slow,
                          Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, CC, PC, PRAM,
                           Causal]
